# Advanced checking-test analysis

Auto-generated by advanced_analysis.py. Departure counts match the workbook measures for 100% of KAC trials (same tracks, zone and 1 s rule).

Rule: any departure (>= 1 s outside the platform zone) means the rat left. KAC: same rats at standard (day 6, 1.5 cm) and raised water (day 8, 3 cm), fixed order. SP1: raised water only.

## Time to first departure

| Contrast | Test | Result | p |
|---|---|---|---|
| SP1 raised | Log-rank, females vs males | chi2 = 12.23 | p < 0.001 |
| KAC standard (1.5 cm) | Log-rank, females vs males | chi2 = 8.39 | p = 0.004 |
| KAC raised (3 cm) | Log-rank, females vs males | chi2 = 23.88 | p < 0.001 |

## Cox model, KAC (robust SE by rat)

| Contrast | Test | Result | p |
|---|---|---|---|
| Female (vs male) | Hazard ratio for leaving | HR = 10.55 (95% CI 3.54-31.37) | p < 0.001 |
| Raised water (vs standard) | Hazard ratio for leaving | HR = 1.49 (95% CI 0.85-2.59) | p = 0.160 |

